I replaced the element-wise vector copies with O(1) swaps that steal the source buffers, eliminating per-field heap allocations and FitValue copy-constructor calls during message construction and vector reallocation.

```cpp
FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
{
    values.swap(const_cast<std::vector<FitValue> &>(field.values));
    stringIndexes.swap(const_cast<std::vector<FIT_STRING_INDEX> &>(field.stringIndexes));
}
```